       Routines that return pointers return NNUULLLL on error, and  set  eerrrrnnoo  to
       the  corresponding  error-code returned by functions returning an inte‐
       ger.  Routines that return an integer return one of the following error
       codes:

       EE__OOKK The routine succeeded.

       EE__BBAADD__AARRGGUUMMEENNTT
            Routine detected an incorrect or out-of-range argument.

       EE__BBAADD__SSTTAATTEE
            Routine was called from an initialization or termination function.

       EE__CCOONNNNEECCTTEEDD
            The field is already connected to a form.

       EE__IINNVVAALLIIDD__FFIIEELLDD
            Contents of a field are not valid.

       EE__NNOOTT__CCOONNNNEECCTTEEDD
            No fields are connected to the form.

       EE__NNOOTT__PPOOSSTTEEDD
            The form has not been posted.

       EE__NNOO__RROOOOMM
            Form is too large for its window.

       EE__PPOOSSTTEEDD
            The form is already posted.

       EE__RREEQQUUEESSTT__DDEENNIIEEDD
            The form driver could not process the request.

       EE__SSYYSSTTEEMM__EERRRROORR
            System error occurred (see eerrrrnnoo(3)).

       EE__UUNNKKNNOOWWNN__CCOOMMMMAANNDD
            The form driver code saw an unknown request code.

